# First Notes on String 6 (repertoire plan: st-first-notes-string-6). An original study on the
# thickest string: E (open), F (fret 1, finger 1) and G (fret 3, finger 3), in quarter and half
# notes. The teacher strums E minor and F on the four thin strings, a Spanish-sounding pair (E
# Phrygian colour): the half step E-F in the tune is the same half step that moves the chords.
# Beats 1 and 3 always land on a note of the chord (E or G over Em, F over F); the other notes
# step between them. Bars 7-8 close with F to Em, the Phrygian cadence, and the tune ends on E.
